# ConfTamer: log grpc-go's server side. Two ways a grpc.Server serves:
# - Server.ServeHTTP (e.g. etcd's grpcHandlerFunc on a TLS listener's http.ServeMux): net/http (or x/net's HTTP/2
#   server, patched by x-net-http2-server.sh) logs "Request received" and "Response sent"; this patch logs the
#   method dispatch as "Request routed" (without it, every method gets the mux's pattern, "/").
# - Server.Serve, grpc-go's own HTTP/2 server (internal/transport/http2_server.go), which net/http never sees: this
#   patch gives each stream a context ID and its connection, and logs all three events, with the method's handler.
# Both log the same events and labels. Applies to google.golang.org/grpc (made against v1.59.0; also applies to
# v1.65.0, kube-apiserver's vendored copy, with offsets); paths are relative to the module root (patch -p1).
# Requires the go-inlibrary.patch toolchain (http.ConftamerLogRouted, and the plain-argument server hooks:
# http.ConftamerServerContext, ConftamerLogServerReceived, ConftamerLogServerRouted, ConftamerLogServerResponse).

